      "level": "Menengah",
      "title": "The Old Lighthouse on the Hill",
      "body": [
        "When I was a boy, my grandpa worked as a lighthouse keeper. The lighthouse stood on a rocky hill by the sea, about one kilometer from our village. Every evening, Grandpa climbed one hundred and twenty steps to light the big lamp at the top.",
        "The lamp was very important. It warned ships about the dangerous rocks under the water. Grandpa never missed a single night, not even when he was sick. 'The ships depend on my light,' he always said.",
        "One stormy night, Grandpa saw a small fishing boat moving toward the rocks. He flashed the lamp three times, and the boat turned away just in time. The next day, the fishermen visited him with a basket of fish to say thank you. Grandpa smiled and said he had only done his job."
      ],
      "gloss": {
